    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形) – rice kernels without husk. The character 粟, by contrast, refers to rice kernels with husk. According to Li Xiaoding (李孝定), the horizontal stroke is a bamboo sieve (籭 or 篩子). See also the bottom component of 暴 in its original form.\nUnrelated to 木, 禾, and 来.\nFrom Proto-Sino-Tibetan *mej (“grain”). Cognate with Garo mi (“rice”), Atong (India) mai (“rice”), Jingpho ma (“rice; paddy”), Rabha মাই (mai), Dimasa mai."
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Short for 米突 (mǐtū), from French mètre."
    }
  ],
